{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/853806-did-the-lunars-ever-try-anything-like-the-cult-of-the-illuminated","id":853806,"title":"Did the Lunars ever try anything like the Cult of the Illuminated?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-26T19:13:19-07:00","id":853806,"title":"Did the Lunars ever try anything like the Cult of the Illuminated?","content":"So the Lunars are probably as well aware as the Sidereals of the returning Solar Exalted, but I don't recall them organising any effort to recruit and train impressionable, just Exalted Solars.<br /> <br /> Am I just misremembering or is there an in lore reason they are ignoring this potent resource?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T19:32:31-07:00","id":853814,"title":"","content":"Lack of access has always been a big thing. In past eds, the Lunars were pushed to the edges of the world, and focused on keeping their culture alive, as well as continuing to resist the Realm. They just didn't have the same access to easy transit that Sidereals did as well, being basically locked out of Yu-Shan.<br /> <br /> In 3e, they're very much active in the world doing guerrilla warfare all over the world against them Realm, and this is more their main focal point than anything else. <br /> <br /> There certainly also is somewhat of a notion that the Sidereals are institutional, and probably are better at creating little projects like that since they have persistently had somewhat of a pro-Solar (to some degree) camp, which isn't a thing for 3e Lunars and didn't make sense for them anyway in past eds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T19:44:18-07:00","id":853824,"title":"","content":"Also it doesn't help that most of the Elder Lunars probably have some form of PTSD from the First Age solars and have no desire to recreate the scenario. The younger Lunars who don't have first age/first hand knowledge of Solar power might be open to the concept, but if you look at the mechanics available to them, the Lunars can't really offer much to a Solar in the way of training.<br /> <br /> At best Lunars could offer a relatively safe base of operations for the Solars to use, though that comes with the issue that the Lunar will eventually lose their command over their subjects due to the power of Solar social and rulership charms. Additionally the solars will cause enough trouble that a legion or two will be sent to stop them and the Lunars city state can't really get out of the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T19:52:08-07:00","id":853826,"title":"","content":"I don't doubt that some Lunars have tried, but I think that large groups have probably had that as a debate point. As Zelb says the Sids have more of an institutionalized power base they can use to more easily ,and safely, try things like the Cult of the Illuminated . Whereas the Silver Pact in 3rd is ,to my knowledge, the largest Lunar organization on the planet and even that's mostly a promise to help one another if the crap hits the fan. <br /> <br /> From the looks of the entry on the pact , and the Lunar entry, it seems that the Lunars generally are aware of the fact that a Solar who's had time to entrench itself and build a base is a nightmare to remove and stop if that becomes necessary. So probably a bit of resistance towards giving them a base to start with. <br /> <br /> That being said I wouldn't be surprised if some groups of Lunars or war dominions tried to set up something similar to the Cult as a means of drawing in young Solars and figuring out what to do with them. Whether that be execute it before it can grow in power, give it training with hopes that it can be useful, or point it in the direction of a problem and figure out how to deal with whatever is still standing when the smoke clears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T21:25:37-07:00","id":853877,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I can see the point about Elder Lunars being reluctant, but as to most of the Lunars born after the usurpation, I'd think that the availability of such a thing as a young Solar would be a very tempting proposition.<br /> <br /> That said, the points about the Sidereals and Young Solars usurping power is well taken. If there is any training it might be one on one (fits the mythic archetype of a swordsman learning from a Tengu, Luke from Yoda or Abe no Seimei's Mom being a nine tailed fox)<br /> <br /> No push to make it an institutionalised thing like the Cult, but as a character background for a Solar with a few dots in Mentor, I think it has merit..,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T23:37:24-07:00","id":853920,"title":"","content":"Actually, it is briefly mentioned that a few of the Elders are trying to.<br /> The organisation in question? The Sun King Seneschals.<br /> <br /> So, for 1500 years, the Solars were essentially gone. The chance of meeting your Solar mate was virtually nill. And yet the Sun King Seneschals fought the Realm in their name. Why? Because it was a useful ideological battle cry. Revenge for the Solars. Tell young Lunars &quot;you would have a perfect, holy, god-king hero as your mate, but the Realm stole it from you, the Dragonblood destroyed utopia.&quot; Not to say the members didn't believe that, but essentially, the organisation's purpose was fighting the Realm: Solar veneration was more a religious/ideological thing than a practical thing, because there just wasn't any Solars.<br /> <br /> But... suddenly the Solars are back. For the young members, great, their prophecied lover of 100 lives has returned, it's time to rebuild utopia. But the Elders are wiser, cannier, and more cynical. Do they really want to be slaves to the Solars? To fight under Solar command, when for 1500 years they've been running things just fine on their own? Do they really want to return to number 2, especially under Exalts who are just a few years old? Not to mention that it turns out that just because the Solars are mighty shining warriors... that doesn't mean they're necessarily moral. Or sane. Or wise.<br /> So, it was mentioned in one book (I forget which) that some of the Sun King Seneschal elders are thinking it's time to bring the Solars in (using their Lunar mates to do so), to get them firmly under the Lunars' control before they put the Lunars under the Solars control. Train them up the way the Sidereals do, to take advice from the caring Lunar elders who just want to help them out, to learn about the evils of the Realm and how beastmen are totally lovely, and that the Usurpation was ultimately the fault of the Sidereals (so you definitely can't trust the so-called &quot;Gold&quot; faction).<br /> <br /> Of course, I wouldn't be surprised if the Sun King Seneschals (and all the other factions) simply don't exist in 3e. But I could still definitely imagine a Lunar elder deciding she needs to take a naive young Solar under her wing so as to mould him into her loyal apprentice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-27-2016, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T03:22:59-07:00","id":853957,"title":"","content":"I think Third Edition is going with the idea that many Lunars from after the Usurpation would be extremely wary of Solars, out of concern for their liberty being infringed upon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T03:57:19-07:00","id":853964,"title":"","content":"I imagine that'd lead to a wide variety of responses, from killing them on sight, through avoiding them, through wary alliance, to trying to appear as their friends in order to influence them, to simply putting them under themselves in a tribe or other organisation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T05:32:42-07:00","id":853982,"title":"","content":"When it comes to cults, Lunars are generally at the centers of any cult they are involved in, I would imagine, at least in terms of 3e. Theirs is not the path of the invisible manipulator in the same way the Sidereals' is (that's not to say they <i>cannot</i> do invisible manipulations of a society, only that it's not quite the same theme), but rather of the glorious god-beast that will lead your tribe to victory against those accursed settled puppets of the Realm! <br /> <br /> At least, that's my perspective. In my vision of Creation, one is not likely to see a Lunar being <i>subtle</i> about backing a cult. The cult <i>itself</i> may be subtle, but the cultists are most likely going to have seen and marveled at the glorious divinity that is the Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T07:11:14-07:00","id":854009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>*End</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/853806-did-the-lunars-ever-try-anything-like-the-cult-of-the-illuminated?p=853982#post853982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes to cults, Lunars are generally at the centers of any cult they are involved in, I would imagine, at least in terms of 3e. Theirs is not the path of the invisible manipulator in the same way the Sidereals' is (that's not to say they <i>cannot</i> do invisible manipulations of a society, only that it's not quite the same theme), but rather of the glorious god-beast that will lead your tribe to victory against those accursed settled puppets of the Realm!<br /> <br /> At least, that's my perspective. In my vision of Creation, one is not likely to see a Lunar being <i>subtle</i> about backing a cult. The cult <i>itself</i> may be subtle, but the cultists are most likely going to have seen and marveled at the glorious divinity that is the Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tammuz and Silver Python &amp; Rain Deathflyer actually make quite good canon examples of them actually playing <b>exactly</b> that role, but the Lunar barbarian god/beast-king can certainly be said to be more of a iconic image for them with the fanbase as a whole indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-10-2016, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T07:21:28-07:00","id":854014,"title":"","content":"It also strikes me that it is probably the inherently subtle or manipulative Lunars (Tammuz, Rain Deathflyer, e.t.c.) that will want to maneuver/mould impressionable young Solars into a weapon to strike at their foes.<br /> <br /> Can you see Strength of Many try something like this?<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T07:23:59-07:00","id":854015,"title":"","content":"Deep ambivalence toward the idea of Solar hegemony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T07:26:13-07:00","id":854016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/853806-did-the-lunars-ever-try-anything-like-the-cult-of-the-illuminated?p=854009#post854009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tammuz and Silver Python &amp; Rain Deathflyer actually make quite good canon examples of them actually playing exactly that role, but the Lunar barbarian god/beast-king can certainly be said to be more of a iconic image for them woth the fanbase as a whole indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, but that was a facet of the part of Lunars in 2e that seems to be not so large a part of their depiction in 3e, from what I recall of the dev's comments in the past. I mean, I agree, those are all pretty good examples of the Lunars being subtle, but I'm not sure that they'll be remaining in that role in the future.<br /> <br /> That said, I would say that if you're looking at them from the perspective of 2e, and are fine with that and all that it entails for your games, then yes, this is totally something that Lunars might do.<br /> <br /> Even in 3e, I can totally see some Lunars sending Solars to smash themselves against the Realm - especially if the Solar in question had been a member of a barbarian group they were <i>already</i> planning to throw at the Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T07:56:29-07:00","id":854033,"title":"","content":"I think that ultimately it is (as others have indicated) a question of different approaches. Sidereals are organizers and indirect actors by nature, so setting up a few hundred or few thousand mortals in an organized structure to help achieve a goal is a thing they might well do. It's playing to their strengths, and while there are very likely exceptions it's the general trend. Lunars on the other hand, don't have the same strengths, so while you're going to get some exceptions that do this kind of thing, they're most likely going to be playing to their own strengths in how they interact with the Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T08:17:37-07:00","id":854046,"title":"","content":"I think having a particular Mentor, with a 1-on-1 relationship in the backstory, rather than an entire faction of Lunars happily saying &quot;we're not worthy, plz oppress me Solar-senpaiiiiiiiii!&quot; is a much better take on the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T13:14:24-07:00","id":854180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/853806-did-the-lunars-ever-try-anything-like-the-cult-of-the-illuminated?p=854046#post854046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think having a particular Mentor, with a 1-on-1 relationship in the backstory, rather than an entire faction of Lunars happily saying &quot;we're not worthy, plz oppress me Solar-senpaiiiiiiiii!&quot; is a much better take on the idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that what the OP is talking about, though?<br /> <br /> It seems to me there's a huge difference between a faction of Lunars who is like &quot;yeah, lets restore the Solar Deliberative, a governing body in which we exercised no power, woo!&quot; and a faction of Lunars who is like &quot;okay, the Solars are back, and they're in the same boat as we are. We should probably make an organized attempt to recruit them into our Forever War against the Realm and the Sidereals, but we will be the senior partners in that alliance by dint of age and experience if nothing else, and assuming we win, Creation thereafter will be ruled by co-equal Celestial Exalts and not a bunch of golden jackasses.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T16:13:28-07:00","id":854241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/853806-did-the-lunars-ever-try-anything-like-the-cult-of-the-illuminated?p=854180#post854180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that what the OP is talking about, though?<br /> <br /> It seems to me there's a huge difference between a faction of Lunars who is like &quot;yeah, lets restore the Solar Deliberative, a governing body in which we exercised no power, woo!&quot; and a faction of Lunars who is like &quot;okay, the Solars are back, and they're in the same boat as we are. We should probably make an organized attempt to recruit them into our Forever War against the Realm and the Sidereals, but we will be the senior partners in that alliance by dint of age and experience if nothing else, and assuming we win, Creation thereafter will be ruled by co-equal Celestial Exalts and not a bunch of golden jackasses.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And this approach will surely have its own set of problems, but it is full of the standard themes for Exalted. Arrogance, dominance, and myopia. Love it.<br /> <br /> That being said, Lunars aren't that organized, so I don't think CoI is the model to use. It's more likely that a few dozen Lunars here and there operate an underground railroad and training network for young Solars. Find them, save their bacon, make them scary, and then unleash them on the Realm.<br /> <br /> In this way, it wouldn't be too far removed from the way Lunars manage war dominions.<br /> <br /> I see two pitfalls to avoid.<br /> 1. Orienting Lunars as a group completely around Solars.<br /> 2. Making Lunar tutelage the obvious best choice, or a complete trap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T16:47:09-07:00","id":854247,"title":"","content":"Huh; a developer quote that doesn't get immediately seized upon and dissected. Curious...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T18:42:04-07:00","id":854299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/853806-did-the-lunars-ever-try-anything-like-the-cult-of-the-illuminated?p=854247#post854247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh; a developer quote that doesn't get immediately seized upon and dissected. Curious...</div> </div> </div> </div>Holden's quote seemed so obvious and banal I personally felt no need to address it. Of course the Lunars are deeply ambivalent about Solar hegemony. <i>The Gold Faction</i> is deeply ambivalent about Solar hegemony and they're actively trying to restore it, so one can only imagine Lunar feelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T22:57:11-07:00","id":854367,"title":"","content":"IIRC, 3e basically take the &quot;Lunar/Solar bond&quot; aspect of the relationship out behind the woodshed and shoots it in the head. So any premise that starts with, &quot;Oh Lunars want/hate their mates&quot; is no longer valid.<br /> <br /> Lacking access to the Loom of Fate makes it difficult to find or track Solar Exalts. Even if Lunars want to raise up Solars, they need to put in a lot more legwork to find them than Sidereals do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T23:06:22-07:00","id":854369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/853806-did-the-lunars-ever-try-anything-like-the-cult-of-the-illuminated?p=854180#post854180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that what the OP is talking about, though?<br /> <br /> It seems to me there's a huge difference between a faction of Lunars who is like &quot;yeah, lets restore the Solar Deliberative, a governing body in which we exercised no power, woo!&quot; and a faction of Lunars who is like &quot;okay, the Solars are back, and they're in the same boat as we are. We should probably make an organized attempt to recruit them into our Forever War against the Realm and the Sidereals, but we will be the senior partners in that alliance by dint of age and experience if nothing else, and assuming we win, Creation thereafter will be ruled by co-equal Celestial Exalts and not a bunch of golden jackasses.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>My suspicion is the &quot;organized&quot; aspect is where things would fall down here, since the Lunars seem to have a pretty thin alliance to begin with. The general idea seems to be that most powerful people who remember the Solars either want to kill them to be safe, or to get in on the ground floor and make the Solars dependent on them, but I would imagine the divide between those two camps (as well as arguments over the merits of specific Solars) would be too acrimonious for a group as dispersed and individualistic as the Lunars to do this on a large scale.<br /> <br /> It seems like the sort of thing <i>some</i> Lunars would do for <i>some</i> Solars, but since Lunars seem to stake out their own personal cults and territory more often than not, it might be difficult to combine those into an actual faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T01:13:50-07:00","id":854388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/853806-did-the-lunars-ever-try-anything-like-the-cult-of-the-illuminated?p=854241#post854241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And this approach will surely have its own set of problems, but it is full of the standard themes for Exalted. Arrogance, dominance, and myopia. Love it.<br /> <br /> That being said, Lunars aren't that organized, so I don't think CoI is the model to use. It's more likely that a few dozen Lunars here and there operate an underground railroad and training network for young Solars. Find them, save their bacon, make them scary, and then unleash them on the Realm.<br /> <br /> In this way, it wouldn't be too far removed from the way Lunars manage war dominions.<br /> <br /> I see two pitfalls to avoid.<br /> 1. Orienting Lunars as a group completely around Solars.<br /> 2. Making Lunar tutelage the obvious best choice, or a complete trap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also I feel like that's a pretty huge waste if you manage to get a solar who's willing to do what you say. Especially if he's a twilight inventor tinker or a holy zenith preacher. I'm pretty sure the best thing to do then is bring him with you and get him to help you manage your affairs, whatever those may be, and keep fingers crossed he doesn't turn around and tell you that he's running the show now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T01:45:10-07:00","id":854392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/853806-did-the-lunars-ever-try-anything-like-the-cult-of-the-illuminated?p=854388#post854388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also I feel like that's a pretty huge waste if you manage to get a solar who's willing to do what you say. Especially if he's a twilight inventor tinker or a holy zenith preacher. I'm pretty sure the best thing to do then is bring him with you and get him to help you manage your affairs, whatever those may be, and keep fingers crossed he doesn't turn around and tell you that he's running the show now.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, if your protege is a Night or a Dawn, those are quite easy to weaponise...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T03:21:37-07:00","id":854401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gold Faction is deeply ambivalent about Solar hegemony and they're actively trying to restore it</div> </div> </div> </div> Sensible depictions will not contradict themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T03:42:23-07:00","id":854404,"title":"","content":"Lupo was deeply ambivalent, that's why he set up a drill camp to turn Solars into servants of the people, tough soldiers.<br /> Ayesha Ura just thought it'd be totally awesome, so set up a temple where Solars were worshipped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T03:47:37-07:00","id":854406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/853806-did-the-lunars-ever-try-anything-like-the-cult-of-the-illuminated?p=853920#post853920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, it was mentioned in one book (I forget which) that some of the Sun King Seneschal elders are thinking it's time to bring the Solars in (using their Lunar mates to do so), to get them firmly under the Lunars' control before they put the Lunars under the Solars control. Train them up the way the Sidereals do, to take advice from the caring Lunar elders who just want to help them out, to learn about the evils of the Realm and how beastmen are totally lovely, and that the Usurpation was ultimately the fault of the Sidereals (so you definitely can't trust the so-called &quot;Gold&quot; faction).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I like those guys. Woe to them if they try this approach on the PC in a game, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1673-runelord","name":"Runelord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1673_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T04:02:23-07:00","id":854409,"title":"","content":"Well, that's the same for the Cult of the Illuminated. I mean, the Cult works fine for a background, but PCs don't really join, seriously.<br /> <br /> I did have one PC who went to a camp in the Scavenger Lands for 3 months, because of the sweet training they offered (100xp of Xp debt!). So, they gave him a light touch in terms of propaganda and brainwashing. And it worked, in that he considered himself a member, tried to live a somewhat decent life, and propagated a version of the religion in his state, but he didn't do what Sidereals told him or anything. Because they thought he'd rebel.<br /> <br /> <br /> I actually think the Sun King manipulators could be an interesting way to do a Solar/Lunar game with starting characters. If you want some kind of base and mentor for the Solars (and Lunars), maybe have a Lunar elder in his barbarian lair. She can support the PCs, give them things to do, teach them kung-fu and sorcery and how the Realm is evil and Lunars are awesome... and then maybe, as time goes by, the PCs realise she doesn't care about them, she's just another manipulator.<br /> I mean, generally I'm happy to have PCs just do things themselves (that's the nice thing about Exalted), but if you do want them to start with some kind of structure, it's an interesting way to do it. And less institutional than the Cult of the Illuminated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T05:11:23-07:00","id":854420,"title":"","content":"...I wonder if Holden misused the term &quot;ambivalent&quot;. I wonder if <i>I</i> frequently misuse the term &quot;ambivalent&quot;. Questions for later... <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Cult works fine for a background, but PCs don't really join, seriously</div> </div> </div> </div> Why is that, I wonder?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T05:36:23-07:00","id":854424,"title":"","content":"I actually miswrote that. I should have said PCs don't seriously join.<br /> <br /> But anyway. It's partly because Players hate being controlled.<br /> <br /> But there's also the fact that joining an organisation rather than making your own isn't a very Solar thing.<br /> <br /> I think the Cult is best at attracting PCs when it's less &quot;join our religion&quot; and more &quot;oh great Solar, we've been primed to worship and obey you!&quot; But then... is that really all that interesting? Compared to making your own cult? Not sure it is.<br /> <br /> Which gets to the fact that I think it works much better as a background thing than in-game.<br /> <br /> Saying this, I have used the Cult a fair bit in my game, but possibly not in the way the writers intended. I mean, none of the PCs have gone to train at Kether Rock, because, honestly, what PC wants to go spend 3 years of downtime training?<br /> <br /> Now, go and train with Sidereal kung-fu masters in a month-long training montage, that's different, but joining what's essentially a school for Solars with a 3-4 year curriculum? No, I don't think many PCs (or Solars!) are keen on that. Solars want to change the world now, not in 20 years.<br /> <br /> So... possibly, what I'm saying is that as much as I like Kether Rock, the camps are the least useful parts of the Cult once the game has started.<br /> <br /> But, hey, there's lots of things that are mainly there for background, maybe that's okay. And it can work well as an organised group of antagonists (for example, barbarian tribes are being united by the 6 fanatical Solars of Kether Rock, you must try and stop them).<br /> <br /> I actually have 5 Solar ex-members of Kether Rock as an antagonist group in my game, who realised the Sidereals were manipulating them and decided to make their own religion. I have always wanted to have a Solar circle of god-kings as antagonists.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T06:16:31-07:00","id":854443,"title":"","content":"I think they called it The Golden Widow Society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T06:32:43-07:00","id":854448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/853806-did-the-lunars-ever-try-anything-like-the-cult-of-the-illuminated?p=854420#post854420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I wonder if Holden misused the term &quot;ambivalent&quot;. I wonder if <i>I</i> frequently misuse the term &quot;ambivalent&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so? Ambivalent means, well, ambivalent; I read &quot;Deep ambivalence towards the idea of Solar hegemony&quot; as &quot;the Lunars are deeply conflicted over the idea, desiring and fearing it in equal measure, and these desires and fears sometimes occur within the same Lunar.&quot;<br /> <br /> And that seems reasonable, for both the Lunars and, for that matter, the Gold Faction? The height of the First Age, before the Solars went batshit, was a glorious time for the Lunars! They stood beside the Solars at the pinnacle of Creation! More prosaically, they bestrode the world like the glorious Chosen of Luna they are, instead of being forced out to to the fringes and locked into an endless war with the Sidereal and Terrestrial Exalted. Indeed, the Terrestrials and Sidereals <i>served</i> them. Why wouldn't you want that back?<br /> <br /> But by the same token, they were also firmly wrapped around the thumbs of the Solars, especially by the end. The Solars went totally bananaballs, and the Lunars were right up there with them while that was happening and they did precisely jack and shit about it. The remaining First Age Lunars probably look back on some of the horror shows they witnessed and have come to the conclusion that the Solars must have been fucking with them as well, because if someone tried that shit in front of them today they'd rip their goddamn throats out. It was legitimately sickhouse. Why the hell would you ever want <i>that</i> back?<br /> <br /> It's perfectly reasonable that there are going to be plenty of Lunars who hew more strongly towards one of these viewpoints than the other, thus generating deep ambivalence within the community of Lunars as a whole, and plenty of Lunars who perceive both these viewpoints as equally strong, thus generating deep ambivalence within individual Lunars. And of course there will be other competing viewpoints as well.<br /> <br /> And that's before you even get into the Gold Faction, who are equally as ambivalent, indeed, one might go as far as to say &quot;schizophrenic&quot; towards the Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T07:56:13-07:00","id":854476,"title":"","content":"I find it interesting that no one has mentioned one of the key advantages the Sidereals have in this is that they are usually able to control the circumstances in which they meet Solars and more importantly have few preconceptions to counter.<br /> From my understanding only a handful of Solars remember Sidereals and of those only a few are distrustful of them (Swan and Sayn are examples). Most Solars only know what the Sidereals tell them about themselves and they capitalize on their abilities to arrange the meetings, a good example of this would be Zelia and Jiunan.<br /> Lunars on the other hand DO have quite a few misconceptions to fight, they are a known quantity and understandably feared by large swaths of Creation (where many Solars Exalt). Even many of the Solars from the caste books who remember Lunars show alternating feelings of fear, sorrow and confusion in regards to what their former friends/lovers/lieutenants have become.<br /> So ya it may be worth considering that a Solars gut reaction to meeting a Lunar may be less &quot;hello future slave&quot; and more &quot;OMG my ex is a were-monster kill it with fire&quot; (that last quote was from a PC from one of my first sessions).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T08:56:57-07:00","id":854501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's partly because Players hate being controlled.</div> </div> </div> </div> Pfft; babies. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">joining an organisation rather than making your own isn't a very Solar thing</div> </div> </div> </div> To be sure, being compelled by the ideas of others, who aren't even your Dad, is so passe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T09:30:59-07:00","id":854516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/853806-did-the-lunars-ever-try-anything-like-the-cult-of-the-illuminated?p=854388#post854388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also I feel like that's a pretty huge waste if you manage to get a solar who's willing to do what you say. Especially if he's a twilight inventor tinker or a holy zenith preacher. I'm pretty sure the best thing to do then is bring him with you and get him to help you manage your affairs, whatever those may be, and keep fingers crossed he doesn't turn around and tell you that he's running the show now.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm sure many Solar-friendly Lunars will reach that conclusion as well; it's a quite reasonable one. Differing approaches will generate conflict within the loose Lunar coalition. Conflict is, of course, the genesis of good stories and campaigns.<br /> <br /> I also second the notion that players don't like being controlled, which is why it's incumbent on the ST (as it often is in Exalted) to use all potential mentor/authority figures with a large dollop of finesse. Generally, players in RPGs want to act, rather than be told. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T09:59:37-07:00","id":854527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/853806-did-the-lunars-ever-try-anything-like-the-cult-of-the-illuminated?p=854424#post854424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually miswrote that. I should have said PCs don't seriously join.<br /> <br /> But anyway. It's partly because Players hate being controlled.<br /> <br /> But there's also the fact that joining an organisation rather than making your own isn't a very Solar thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like there's a lot of room to make the Cult an appealing PC backer or basis for a campaign, given the popularity of 1e Abyssals, who were very Solar-like in scope but basically had a CotI thing going except with a shorter leash and everyone a jerk. The writing has never done a very good job pitching the Cult, and I think that if that changed it'd be a different story. People <i>don't</i> like being controlled, generally, but they <i>do</i> like getting lots of support and free stuff, and oftentimes they also like getting embroiled in webs of intrigue and deceit, because that's the social equivalent of a ninja battle. But the Cult needs to make itself more intrinsically appealing as a game focus for that angle to work well. I remember Holden saying that if 2e had continued there were plans to do a Cult book, and I would have been interested to see that.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T18:17:15-07:00","id":854774,"title":"","content":"I would have loved to see a 2E Cult book. I would like to know what sort of changes the writers had time to cook up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T04:18:33-07:00","id":854982,"title":"","content":"I always thought of cult of ilumineted as attempt to <br /> impose certain belief and policies on emerging solar <br /> society and as tool to find and gather new solars.<br /> This organisation plays on sidereal strong points: <br /> very good influence in the threshold, much better <br /> cooperation and organisation as sidereal society <br /> than lunar one.<br /> Lunar themes are self reliance it does not fit <br /> creation organisation much bigger than any random <br /> elder or group of elders. To create something <br /> aproaching cult they would have to become much <br /> more organised coodependant (and vulnerable).. <br /> sonething they decided not to do as presented in the<br /> setting. So some elder may help solar or circle but <br /> won't commi to anything bigger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4588-ludek","name":"Ludek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}